Package: ggsynteny
Type: Package
Title: Publication-Quality Synteny Plots with 'ggplot2'
Version: 0.5.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Loukas", "Theodosiou", email = "loukesio@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-6418-4652"))
Description: Create publication-quality synteny plots for comparative genomics.
    Supports both macro-synteny (chromosome-level) and micro-synteny (gene-level)
    visualizations with flexible coloring schemes, including the 32 palettes of
    the 'ltc' package usable by name (e.g. palette = "casa_natal"). Includes
    parsers for common synteny file formats including MCScanX, GENESPACE, and
    custom TSV formats. Circular chromosome and gene views use native 'ggplot2'
    layers to connect genomic intervals with chord ribbons. An optional Shiny
    app previews uploaded results and exports figures and the displayed data.
    Reference comparison rings display supplied variant calls and optional
    alignment identity windows for one or more comparison genomes.
